course: dictionary
lesson: 16063
title: Void: empty, missing, cancelled
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Void has more than one meaning, so context matters. Read the words around it. «The rocket drifted slowly through the dark void of space.» The clues are rocket, dark and space, so void means a completely empty space.
explain: «The shop said her ticket was void because the date had passed.» The clues are ticket and date passed. Void means no longer valid, so the ticket cannot be used. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The ticket cannot be used" fits, so you are right.
explain: Void can also be a feeling. «After her best friend moved away, Mia felt a void in her day.» The clue is the missing friend. Here void means that something important is missing.
fact: A void is a completely empty space, like the space between stars.
fact: «Void» can also mean a feeling that something important is missing, especially after losing someone.
fact: In law, «void» means no longer valid, so «null and void» means cancelled and having no effect.
fact: To void something means to cancel it officially, and «void of» means completely without something, as in «a sky void of clouds».
fact: Use the clues to choose the meaning: space, a ticket, or a missing feeling each point to a different meaning.
exercise: «The rocket drifted slowly through the cold void.» What does void mean here? | *A completely empty space | A large, wet field | A warm, cosy room | A loud crowd of people
exercise: «Her ticket was void because the date had passed.» What does void mean here? | *No longer valid, so it cannot be used | Brightly coloured | Lost in the post | Very, very cheap
exercise: What does it mean to void a contract? | *To cancel it officially | To read it aloud | To copy it neatly | To sign it in gold ink
test: «After her best friend moved away, Mia felt a void in her day.» What does void mean here? | A loud noise | A tiny hole in the wall | A happy holiday | *A feeling that something important is missing
test: Complete the sentence: «The sky was ___ clouds.» | voided | voiding | voids | *void of
exam: Ben reads «The contract was null and void.» What does void mean here? | Very large | *No longer valid, so it has no effect | Filled with water | Painted in bright colours
